# Reference only. The guided first run creates a minimal .env containing the selected provider.
# Copy to .env, keep it git-ignored, and leave every unused key absent rather than blank.

# Add only when the connected Traigent run is about to start.
# Portal API keys begin with uk_.
TRAIGENT_API_KEY=

# Choose ONE provider section. OpenRouter is a convenient default because one key reaches
# multiple model vendors. OpenRouter is the gateway; the upstream inference provider may also
# receive prompts/examples/outputs. Record every allowed upstream
# provider/route and fallback policy in the combined approval; pin routes and disable fallbacks
# when an exact recipient set is required.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Alternatives - replace the OpenRouter line with exactly one of these when selected.
# If exactly one of these already holds a key, the walkthrough uses that provider directly,
# so no OpenRouter account is needed.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# COHERE_API_KEY=

# Leave cost settings absent. The assistant uses the installed SDK's per-optimization default and
# one `$5.00` total walkthrough ceiling unless the paid-work approval states otherwise.
# Never persist TRAIGENT_COST_APPROVED here; approval applies only to the current run process.
